From 637d2a5539a2e7721149b2f78669f2c21c6b520c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RNVizion <vizionaryfx@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:59:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] refuse an unknown harmony scheme or text operation
 instead of defaulting

generate_harmony returned [base] for a scheme it did not know and
transform_text returned the input unchanged for an operation it did not
know. Both fail open: a one-colour "harmony" for a typo, and a `result`
that reads like success and is not. Both reproduced on the live server
2026-09-27 ("tridic", "uppercase"). mix_colors and convert_color already
refuse an unknown selector at the api seam; these two now do the same,
naming the choice list.

- engine/color_harmony.py: the by-name table is hoisted to HARMONY_SCHEMES
  so the api refuses against the table the engine dispatches on (one list,
  not a copy). The engine's own [base] fallback is kept for the desktop
  GUI's contract and documented as not relied on here.
- api.py: transform_text folds case on the selector, which is resolution
  not guessing because the folded spellings are unique (a test pins that);
  whitespace normalization stays parked with alias normalization.
- tests/test_selector_refusals.py (11): named positive control, both
  refusals with their lists, the hand-transcribed scheme/operation copies
  held to equality against the engine.

Each guard was broken deliberately and failed for the named reason.
Suite 44 -> 55 on 3.12 and 3.13.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01McgAPxvtUNHD5Z46jfvF3o
