From 786d5de6748f50719e506bb84f487d857ccbb489 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RNVizion <vizionaryfx@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:59:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] save_palette resolves every colour and refuses a name the
 resolver cannot reach

Two defects on the one write path, found 2026-09-27.

The store held whatever it was handed. The live store's "Test Colors"
carried the strings "Purple" and "Green" as swatches, and referencing one
failed with `invalid literal for int() with base 16: 'Pu'` -- no reason,
no location. Now every colour is resolved through the same resolver the
other nine tools use (hex, CSS name, brand name, palette reference) and
stored as normalized #rrggbb; an unknown token refuses the whole save
naming its position. Resolution happens at save time, so a saved palette
is a snapshot, which is what it is for. A malformed swatch already in the
store refuses by palette, position and value (engine/resolve.py) and says
to re-save; it is not resolved leniently on the way out, because a store
holding a non-hex swatch is wrong and a lenient read would hide it forever.

Saved palettes resolve ahead of brand and CSS names, and the public
endpoint runs auth-off, so one save_palette("brand gold", ["#ff0000"])
redefined that name for every caller, durably. The write path now refuses
a name that is a brand key, a CSS name, a "css:" form, a hex literal, or
contains ":" (the swatch separator), each with its reason. Resolution
order is unchanged; the collision is refused at the only place it could
be created. Every name the live store held on 2026-09-27 is still allowed
(a control pins that).

- engine/resolve.py: normalize_hex made public; _from_palette refuses a
  non-hex stored swatch by name; shadowing note added to the docstring.
- api.py: resolution and the reserved-name check at the seam; the
  `colors` and `name` Field descriptions say so.
- server.py: the save_palette description says so (model-facing text).
- tests/test_palette_contract.py (19): named positive control, the
  production case, the legacy-store refusal through four tools, the
  reserved-name matrix, the not-over-broad control.

Each guard was broken deliberately and failed for the named reason.
Suite 55 -> 74 on 3.12 and 3.13.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01McgAPxvtUNHD5Z46jfvF3o
