From 89a883d13957e6255c6dce0370292616f86b4544 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RNVizion <vizionaryfx@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:00:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] never push over the Dataset after a failed hydrate; say
 why a save is not durable

Hydration at startup is what makes a best-effort push safe: the local
file is a superset of the Dataset only if the Dataset was read first. The
hydrate step was one bare `except: pass`, so any transient failure at
boot -- network, rate limit, a copy that failed -- started the store
empty AND ready, and the next save would have pushed a one-palette
palettes.json over every palette the Dataset held. Not observed in
production; the window is real on every rebuild.

Three startup outcomes now, and only two make a durable writer:
hydrated, or a CONFIRMED "no palettes.json yet" (EntryNotFoundError).
Anything else is "could not look": the store stays local-only for the
life of the process and every save reports durable=False with the reason.

The hub's own exception hierarchy carries the trap: LocalEntryNotFoundError
("the network did not answer; the entry may exist on the Hub") SUBCLASSES
EntryNotFoundError. Caught parent-first, an outage files as an empty
Dataset. The store checks the subclass first and the test pins that
order -- breaking it flipped `durable` to True on an outage, which is the
exact clobber.

- engine/palette_store.py: the split, and `durable_reason` on the store,
  set at startup and overwritten by a failed push.
- api.py: SavePaletteResult gains `durable_reason` (additive). A false
  flag with no reason is a shrug; this is the reason.
- server.py: the save_palette description says so.
- tests/test_store_durability.py (12): huggingface_hub faked at the two
  attributes the store imports, no network, no credential; a positive
  control proving the fakes are reached and a normal boot pushes a
  superset; the outage-shaped not-found; three other hydrate failures;
  unreachable at startup; a failed push keeps the local save and the next
  good push clears the reason.

Each guard was broken deliberately and failed for the named reason,
including restoring the old bare except. Suite 74 -> 86 on 3.12 and 3.13.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01McgAPxvtUNHD5Z46jfvF3o
